		<main id="page-main" class="layout-main">    <div role="main" id="primary-content" class="content-primary content-primary--secondary-none content-primary--full-width-contained content-primary--has-body-sidebar">
                <article id="post-3087" class="post-3087 reports type-reports status-publish has-post-thumbnail hentry company-114">
                
                <header class="content-primary__header content-primary__header--featured-image-background bg-3091">
                    <div class="container">
                        <h1 class="content-primary__title">MW is Short NVIDIA: More Questions About China (NVDA US)</h1>
                    </div>
                    <style>
		

		.no-js .bg-3091, .no-mq .bg-3091 {background-image:url('https://muddywatersresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/nvda_logo.jpg');}
		
		@media only screen and (max-width: 400px) {
          .bg-3091 {background-image:url('https://muddywatersresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/nvda_logo-400x200.jpg')}
        }
		@media only screen and (min-width: 401px) and (max-width: 800px) {
          .bg-3091 {background-image:url('https://muddywatersresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/nvda_logo.jpg')}
        }
		@media only screen and (min-width: 801px) and (max-width: 1600px) {
          .bg-3091 {background-image:url('https://muddywatersresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/nvda_logo.jpg')}
        }
        @media only screen and (min-width: 1601px) {
          .bg-3091 {background-image:url('https://muddywatersresearch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/nvda_logo.jpg')}
        }  
	</style>                </header>
                
                <div class="container content-primary__main-container">
                    <div class="content-primary__main">
                                                <div class="content-primary__body-wrapper">
                            <div class="content-primary__body">
                                <p>Muddy Waters is short NVIDIA (NVDA). A class action suit filed against Super Micro Computer Inc. in October alleges that former SMCI Chief Growth Officer, a woman named Cenly Chen, “managed [SMCI’s] acquisition of GPU chips from NVIDIA” and “decided how to distribute [NVDA GPUs] among Super Micro’s customers.” In March this year, the U.S. indicted three SMCI employees for illegally selling at least approximately $2.5 billion of SMCI servers with NVDA GPUs to end customers in China through a Singapore front company.  Referring to the ex-SMCI executive, the class action complaint alleges that there was “no way Cenly Chen lacked knowledge of [SMCI’s] illicit sales.”</p>
<p>Separately, a woman identified as Cenly Chen, referred to in some photograph tags as Cenly Puri, has been photographed in public between 2024 to 2026 with Ajay K. Puri. Until this June, Mr. Puri was likely the third most senior executive at NVDA, behind only Jensen Huang and Colette Kress. His title was EVP Worldwide Field Operations and his total compensation was slightly above Ms. Kress’ in fiscal years 2024 to 2026. Mr. Puri was one of only five NVDA executives named in the 2026 Proxy.</p>
<p>Mr. Puri left NVDA in late June 2026, and the former SMCI executive named Cenly Chen left SMCI in late April or early May 2026. Mr. Puri continues to serve in a senior advisory role to NVDA.</p>
<p>Nobody by the name of Cenley Chen has been indicted or otherwise accused of criminal conduct by any government. The allegations in the class action are unproven.</p>
<p>The question is whether the woman identified as Cenly Chen or Cenly Puri in photographs with Mr. Puri is the same Cenly Chen formerly employed by SMCI.</p>
                                                            </div>

                                                        <div class="content-primary__body-sidebar" role="complementary">
                                <div class="report__download">
                                    
